---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'October 11, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="Reelay Studio Privacy Policy. Transparent, local-first data architecture. We do not track, harvest, or store your videos, drafts, or API tokens on remote cloud servers."
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <div class="badge badge-brand">Local-First Compliance</div>
        <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last Updated: {lastUpdated} • Version 1.2</p>
      </header>

      <!-- Executive Privacy Summary -->
      <div class="compliance-box">
        <h3 class="compliance-box-title">Executive Summary: Zero Cloud Harvesting</h3>
        <p>
          Reelay Studio is a <strong>local-first desktop software application</strong> developed for macOS and Windows. 
          Unlike traditional web-based social media management SaaS tools:
        </p>
        <ul class="summary-list">
          <li><strong>We do not operate a centralized cloud database</strong> that stores your videos, captions, transcripts, or personal credentials.</li>
          <li><strong>All project data and media files reside strictly on your local computer</strong> in an encrypted or local SQLite database.</li>
          <li><strong>OAuth tokens</strong> (YouTube, Meta, TikTok) are saved exclusively in your operating system's native secure keychain (macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager).</li>
          <li><strong>We do not track, profile, monetize, or train AI models</strong> on your content or personal activity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <h2>1. Who We Are and What Reelay Does</h2>
        <p>
          Reelay ("Reelay Studio", "we", "our", or "us") provides a desktop content operations system designed for video creators. The software runs natively on macOS and Windows, enabling creators to organize raw media assets, preview videos in 16:9 and 9:16 aspect ratios, transcribe speech using offline local AI models (such as Whisper), manage an editorial Kanban board, and publish directly to third-party platforms including YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, Threads, and Facebook.
        </p>

        <h2 id="google-limited-use">2. Google API Services & YouTube Data API Disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          Reelay Studio integrates with Google APIs, specifically the YouTube Data API v3, to allow users to inspect their channel video metadata and publish videos directly from their desktop.
        </p>

        <h3>2.1 Requested Google Scopes</h3>
        <p>Reelay requests the following minimum scopes necessary to provide core publishing functionality:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.upload</code>: Required solely to allow you to upload video files directly from Reelay Studio to your connected YouTube channel.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly</code>: Required solely to query your channel title, playlists, and video upload status to confirm successful publication.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.2 Google API Services User Data Policy Compliance</h3>
        <blockquote>
          Reelay's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </blockquote>
        <p>In strict adherence to these requirements:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No External Transmission:</strong> Information accessed via Google APIs (including your YouTube channel tokens, profile details, and video metadata) is stored locally on your machine and is <strong>never transmitted to, collected by, or stored on Reelay servers</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>No Advertising:</strong> Google user data is never used, transferred, or sold for serving advertisements, retargeting, or credit checks.</li>
          <li><strong>No AI Model Training:</strong> Google user data is never used to train generalized artificial intelligence (AI) or machine learning (ML) models.</li>
          <li><strong>Loopback OAuth Flow:</strong> Google authentication uses standard RFC 8252 OAuth 2.0 loopback redirect on <code>http://127.0.0.1</code>. Your browser connects directly to Google; Reelay never intercepts or acts as a proxy for your Google password or credentials.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.3 Token Revocation and Deletion</h3>
        <p>
          You have full and immediate control over your Google credentials. When you click <strong>"Disconnect"</strong> next to your YouTube account inside Reelay Studio (Settings → Accounts → YouTube):
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>The application immediately calls Google's OAuth 2.0 token revocation endpoint (<code>https://oauth2.googleapis.com/revoke</code>) to permanently invalidate your active refresh and access tokens.</li>
          <li>The tokens are instantly erased from your operating system's native keychain (macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager).</li>
          <li>All local cached metadata for that channel is purged from your local SQLite database.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          You may also revoke Reelay Studio's access at any time via your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account Security Settings</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>2.4 App Review Demo Verification</h3>
        <p>
          For Google Cloud App Review and compliance verification, an unlisted walkthrough of the desktop OAuth loopback sign-in and upload pipeline is available at our <a href="/support#demo-verification">Verification Portal</a> or by contacting <code>compliance@reelay.app</code>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="meta-compliance">3. Meta Platform (Facebook, Instagram & Threads) Disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          Reelay allows creators to cross-post reels and carousel media to Instagram, Facebook Pages, and Threads.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Local SQLite Storage:</strong> All account IDs, Page access tokens, and post staging data reside purely in your personal local SQLite database file on your workstation.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct API Dispatch:</strong> When you schedule or publish a post, Reelay communicates directly between your local IP address and Meta Graph API endpoints (<code>graph.facebook.com</code>). No intermediate Reelay cloud proxy touches your media or payloads.</li>
          <li><strong>User Data Deletion:</strong> As detailed in our dedicated <a href="/data-deletion">User Data Deletion Instructions</a>, disconnecting your account or removing your local application directory deletes 100% of Meta platform tokens and cached data.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. TikTok Developer Platform Disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          Reelay integrates with the TikTok Content Posting API. TikTok OAuth access tokens and video handoff files remain strictly on your local disk. Reelay does not access your personal TikTok direct messages, private contact lists, or financial info. Read and publish permissions are requested purely to enable direct-from-desktop video publishing and verification of upload completion.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Information Collected & Information Not Collected</h2>
        
        <h3>5.1 Information We Do NOT Collect</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>No Video Files or Media Assets:</strong> Your high-resolution 4K video files, audio tracks, and images remain in your chosen local folders. We have zero access to your raw media.</li>
          <li><strong>No Spoken Transcripts or Scripts:</strong> Whisper AI models run on your local CPU/GPU (Apple Silicon Metal / DirectX). Spoken transcripts are indexed in your local SQLite full-text search (FTS5) table and are never sent to our servers.</li>
          <li><strong>No Passwords or Secret Keys:</strong> We never see or store your third-party account passwords or your personal LLM API keys (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini).</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>5.2 Information We May Receive</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Website Visits:</strong> When visiting this marketing site (<code>reelay.app</code>), standard web server logs (IP address, user agent) are processed for basic security and DDoS prevention. No cross-site advertising cookies or behavioral trackers are used.</li>
          <li><strong>Software Updates:</strong> The desktop app checks our public GitHub repository or update manifest for new releases. This check contains only the application version and operating system architecture (e.g., <code>macOS-arm64</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>Direct Inquiries:</strong> If you contact us via email for technical support or bug reports, we retain your email address and message contents solely to resolve your issue.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Third-Party AI Companions & Model Context Protocol (MCP)</h2>
        <p>
          Reelay includes support for the Model Context Protocol (MCP) and OpenAPI tools, allowing users to connect their own AI assistants (such as Claude Desktop, ChatGPT, or Google Gemini).
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Zero Token Reselling or Markup:</strong> Reelay does not resell AI tokens. Connections are established using your own assistant subscriptions or API keys.</li>
          <li><strong>Scoped Security Boundary:</strong> Reelay enforces an un-bypassable security layer (<code>ScopedPipeline</code>). An external AI tool cannot publish, modify account credentials, or delete media without generating a local durable approval request that you must explicitly click to authorize.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Data Security on Your Local Device</h2>
        <p>
          Because Reelay operates locally, the security of your stored tokens and media is protected by your device's operating system security controls:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Keychain Protection:</strong> Sensitive authentication tokens are stored in the macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager, protected by your system login password and biometric authentication (Touch ID / Windows Hello).</li>
          <li><strong>Local Database:</strong> SQLite database files are stored in your user-restricted Application Support folder (<code>~/Library/Application Support/reelay</code> on macOS, <code>%APPDATA%\reelay</code> on Windows) accessible only by your user account.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Contact Us & Data Protection Inquiries</h2>
        <p>
          For questions regarding this Privacy Policy, compliance audits, or platform developer verification, please reach out to our team:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Compliance & App Review Inquiries:</strong> <code>compliance@reelay.app</code></li>
          <li><strong>Privacy & Security Team:</strong> <code>privacy@reelay.app</code></li>
          <li><strong>Physical Address:</strong> Reelay Studio, c/o BeUnconventionalHQ Development Team</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .compliance-box-title {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--brand-light);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .summary-list {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
